export default {"id":"production-level-8","number":8,"title":"Module 8 — Capstone C","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"1. Deliverable 1 must be conceived, arranged, and performed entirely within Session View. 2. You may NOT open Operator, Wavetable, Sampler, or third-party synths to avoid sectional form.","modules":[{"id":"production-m-8-1","code":"8","title":"Session Capstone (Required) · Gate C · Deliverable 1","blurb":"1. Deliverable 1 must be conceived, arranged, and performed entirely within Session View. 2. You may NOT open Operator, Wavetable, Sampler, or third-party synths to avoid sectional form.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"production-l-o-12","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 8 — Session Capstone (Required) · Gate C · Deliverable 1","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Intent:</strong> Synthesize all non-linear Session View composing, clip triggering, scene navigation, and Two-Lever Contrast mechanisms into a completed, professional first song performed live from scenes. Export the 24-bit lossless master WAV, document the formal scene map, maintain source provenance, and achieve <strong>Gate C Certification</strong>.   <strong>Required Capstone Module.</strong> Gate C.   <strong>Strict Pedagogical Invariants:</strong>  "},{"type":"list","items":["Deliverable 1 must be conceived, arranged, and performed entirely within <strong>Session View</strong>.","You may NOT open Operator, Wavetable, Sampler, or third-party synths to avoid sectional form.","Recording an arrangement pass to the ruler is permitted strictly as an archival document—it does NOT constitute Deliverable 2.  "],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Primary Source References:</strong> Ableton Live 12 Reference Manual (Ch. 5: Managing Files, Ch. 7.5: Session/Arrangement Independence); <em>Music-Production-Songwriting-Knowledgebase.md</em> (§1.1, §1.2, §8.7, §9.4, §9.7, §14); Novation Launchkey MK4 User Guide (Clip Mode, Scene Launch); <em>Song Finishing Checklist.pdf</em>."},{"type":"heading","text":"Section 8.1 — Deliverable 1: The Session-Native Master","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section ID:</strong> <code>production-m8-1</code>   <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Select a taught structural convention (Pop Form from Section 1.4–1.8 or an opened Genre Lab).","Build the named Session scene matrix before authoring melodic/percussive content.","Produce exclusively inside Session View clip slots without touching the Arrangement timeline.","Enforce the Two-Lever Contrast rule between verse/chorus or groove/drop scenes.","Perform the complete song form live using Novation Launchkey MK4 scene launch pads.","Render the 24-bit master audio WAV and achieve <strong>Gate C Certification</strong>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-1","title":"8.1.1 — Choosing a Taught Structural Convention (or Pop)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.1 — Choosing a Taught Structural Convention (or Pop)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Select the underlying structural framework for Deliverable 1.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. The Convention Selection Matrix","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Deliverable 1 must adhere strictly to a taught musical form. You may NOT invent an arbitrary structure:"},{"type":"table","headers":["Structural Convention Chosen","Required Scene Matrix Hierarchy","Target Duration / Bars"],"rows":[["<strong>Standard Pop / Radio (Default)</strong>","<code>01_Intro</code>  <code>02_Verse_1</code>  <code>03_Pre_Chorus</code>  <code>04_Chorus_1</code>  <code>05_Verse_2</code>  <code>06_Bridge</code>  <code>07_Final_Chorus</code>  <code>08_Outro</code>","2.0–3.0 min (64–96 bars)"],["<strong>Contemporary R&amp;B (Lab 4.2)</strong>","<code>01_Intro</code>  <code>02_Verse_A</code>  <code>03_Main_Hook</code>  <code>04_Verse_B</code>  <code>05_Space_Break</code>  <code>06_Hook_Adlib</code>  <code>07_Outro</code>","2.5–3.5 min (64–80 bars)"],["<strong>Boom-Bap Hip-Hop (Lab 5.1)</strong>","<code>01_Intro_Chop</code>  <code>02_Verse_16</code>  <code>03_Hook_Chop</code>  <code>04_Verse_16</code>  <code>05_Hook_Chop</code>  <code>06_Outro_Decay</code>","2.0–3.0 min (64–80 bars)"],["<strong>Trap (Lab 5.2)</strong>","<code>01_Atmosphere</code>  <code>02_Verse_808</code>  <code>03_Snare_Roll_Build</code>  <code>04_MAIN_DROP</code>  <code>05_Break</code>  <code>06_DROP_2</code>  <code>07_Outro</code>","2.0–2.5 min (64 bars)"],["<strong>House / Extended Club (Lab 6.1)</strong>","<code>01_DJ_Intro</code>  <code>02_Bass_Groove</code>  <code>03_Vocal_Build</code>  <code>04_MAIN_DROP</code>  <code>05_Breakdown</code>  <code>06_DROP_2</code>  <code>07_DJ_Outro</code>","3.5–5.5 min (96–160 bars)"],["<strong>Dubstep / 140 (Lab 7.1)</strong>","<code>01_Intro</code>  <code>02_Build_140</code>  <code>03_MAIN_DROP_WOBBLE</code>  <code>04_Breakdown</code>  <code>05_DROP_2_CLIMAX</code>  <code>06_Outro</code>","2.5–3.5 min (64–96 bars)"],["<strong>Drum &amp; Bass (Lab 7.2)</strong>","<code>01_Atmosphere</code>  <code>02_Buildup_Ramp</code>  <code>03_AMEN_DROP_174</code>  <code>04_Breakdown</code>  <code>05_REESE_CLIMAX</code>  <code>06_Outro</code>","3.0–4.5 min (96–128 bars)"]],"caption":null},{"type":"list","items":["Document your choice in project notes: <code>D1_CONVENTION = POP_RADIO</code> (or lab code)."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-2","title":"8.1.2 — Authoring the Named Scene List First","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.2 — Authoring the Named Scene List First","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Populate and name all Session Scene rows before generating musical clips.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Pre-Production Scene Scaffolding","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Before recording your first drum or bass clip:"},{"type":"list","items":["Open a blank Live Set.","In the Master Track lane on the far right of Session View, right-click each Scene row  Select <strong>Rename (<code>Ctrl + R</code>)</strong>.","Name all 6 to 8 scenes matching your chosen convention.","<em>Rule</em>: A Session Set with unnamed scene rows (<code>Scene 1</code>, <code>Scene 2</code>, <code>Scene 3</code>) fails Gate C immediately."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-3","title":"8.1.3 — Producing Exclusively Within Session View","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.3 — Producing Exclusively Within Session View","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Confine all creative composition and layering strictly to the Session clip grid.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Non-Linear Production Discipline","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Stay in Session View (<code>Tab</code>).","Compose clips for Drums, Bass, Chords, Leads, and FX across the scene matrix.","Use <strong>Capture MIDI (<code>Ctrl + Shift + C</code>)</strong> to capture improvisations on the Launchkey MK4 without stopping playback.","Maintain stock / Core Library sounds (Live 12 Standard <code>Drift</code>, <code>Electric</code>, <code>Simpler</code>, <code>Drum Rack</code>). Do NOT open Suite tools or complex modular plugins."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-4","title":"8.1.4 — Enforcing the Two-Lever Contrast Rule","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.4 — Enforcing the Two-Lever Contrast Rule","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Verify that adjacent structural scenes exhibit at least two distinct contrast levers.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. The Two-Lever Audit Matrix (Knowledgebase §9.4)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Audition Scene 2 (Verse) vs. Scene 4 (Chorus / Drop):"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Lever 1 (Orchestration Density)</strong>: Verse uses 3 tracks; Chorus unmuted to 7 tracks.","<strong>Lever 2 (Register / Frequency)</strong>: Verse lead plays in Octave 3 (C3–C4); Chorus lead plays in Octave 5 (C5–C6).","<strong>Lever 3 (Rhythmic Division)</strong>: Verse uses closed 8th-note hats; Chorus engages 16th-note open hats and ride cymbal.","<strong>Lever 4 (Stereo Width)</strong>: Verse instruments are centered mono; Chorus synths are hard-panned 45% Left/Right.","<strong>Lever 5 (Harmonic Tension)</strong>: Pre-Chorus ends on an unresolved V7 chord; Chorus resolves to tonic I (or i)."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Rule</em>: At least two of these levers must be physically audible with the Master fader completely static."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-5","title":"8.1.5 — The Novation Launchkey MK4 Radio Performance Pass","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.5 — The Novation Launchkey MK4 Radio Performance Pass","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Perform the complete song arrangement live using hardware scene launch pads.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Hardware Performance Protocol","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Set the Launchkey MK4 61 to <strong>Session / Clip Mode</strong>.","The 2× 8 RGB pads illuminate matching your Session clip colors.","Start playback: Press Scene Launch Button 1 (<code>01_Intro</code>).","Count 8 bars  Launch Scene 2 (<code>02_Verse_1</code>).","Launch subsequent scenes in strict chronological order through the Outro.","Use Launchkey MK4 hardware faders to balance volume levels dynamically during the pass."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-6","title":"8.1.6 — Recording the Arrangement Pass as an Archival Document","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.6 — Recording the Arrangement Pass as an Archival Document","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Capture the live Session performance onto the linear ruler as an archival log.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Archival Recording (Ableton Manual §7.5)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Click the <strong>Arrangement Record Button (<code>●</code>)</strong> in the Control Bar.","Trigger your scene launches live from the Launchkey MK4.","Live writes the real-time performance onto the Arrangement timeline.","<strong>The Archival Invariant</strong>: This recorded pass is strictly an <strong>archival log</strong> (<code>D1_Archive.als</code>). It is NOT Deliverable 2."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-7","title":"8.1.7 — Exporting the 24-Bit Master Audio WAV","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.7 — Exporting the 24-Bit Master Audio WAV","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Render the final lossless master bounce in Live 12 Standard.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Export Configuration Dialogue (Ctrl + Shift + R)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Render Track</strong>: <code>Master</code>","<strong>Render Start</strong>: <code>1.1.1</code> | <strong>Render Length</strong>: Matches full performance duration.","<strong>File Type</strong>: <code>WAV</code> | <strong>Sample Rate</strong>: <code>44100 Hz</code> | <strong>Bit Depth</strong>: <code>24</code>","<strong>Dither Option</strong>: <code>POW-r 3</code> | <strong>Normalize</strong>: <code>Off</code>","<strong>Output Destination</strong>: <code>Deliverable_1_Session_Song/D1_Session_Master_v01.wav</code>"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-8","title":"8.1.8 — Authoring the Formal Scene Launch Map","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.8 — Authoring the Formal Scene Launch Map","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Document the exact scene launch chronology in project notes.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Documentation Requirements","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Create <code>D1_SECTIONS.txt</code> in <code>Deliverable_1_Session_Song/</code>:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">===================================================================\nDELIVERABLE 1: SESSION LAUNCH CHRONOLOGY &amp; SCENE MAP\nCONVENTION: Pop Radio Edit | TEMPO: 122.00 BPM | TOTAL TIME: 2m 45s\n===================================================================\n1. Scene 1: 01_Intro       (8 bars)  [Filtered Keys + Vinyl Crackle]\n2. Scene 2: 02_Verse_1     (16 bars) [Kick + Snare + Bassline + Dry Vocal Lead]\n3. Scene 3: 03_Pre_Chorus  (8 bars)  [Snare Roll + Low-Pass Filter Sweep 400Hz-15kHz]\n4. Scene 4: 04_Chorus_1    (16 bars) [Full Drums + Wide Supersaws + Octave Vocal]\n5. Scene 5: 05_Verse_2     (8 bars)  [Short Verse + 16th Shakers]\n6. Scene 6: 06_Bridge      (8 bars)  [Harmonic shift to relative minor + Drums muted]\n7. Scene 7: 07_Chorus_2    (16 bars) [Double Chorus + Ride Cymbal + Top-Octave Lead]\n8. Scene 8: 08_Outro       (8 bars)  [Subtractive Decay + Reverb Fade]\n===================================================================\nCONTRAST LEVERS VERIFIED:\n- Lever 1: Orchestration Density (Verse: 3 tracks -&gt; Chorus: 7 tracks)\n- Lever 2: Frequency Register (Verse Lead: C3-C4 -&gt; Chorus Lead: C5-C6)\n===================================================================</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-9","title":"8.1.9 — Archival Finalization: Collect All and Save","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.9 — Archival Finalization: Collect All and Save","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Package all project assets into an independent, self-contained project folder.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Archival Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Execute <code>File -&gt; Collect All and Save</code>:"},{"type":"list","items":["Confirm all audio clips are collected into <code>Deliverable_1_Session_Song/Samples/</code>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l8-1-10","title":"8.1.10 — Mistake Canon Audit & Gate C Certification","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"8.1.10 — Mistake Canon Audit & Gate C Certification","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Verify compliance against the master mistake canon and attain Gate C.  "}]},{"type":"step","title":"1. Final Competency Verification","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[x] <strong>No Loop Trap</strong>: Full 8-scene structure completed.","[x] <strong>No Premature Mixing</strong>: Form was locked before fine-tuning EQ/compression.","[x] <strong>No Unnamed Scenes</strong>: Every scene row has an explicit structural name.","[x] <strong>Two-Lever Contrast Verified</strong>: Distinct orchestration and register shifts between verse and chorus.","[x] <strong>Independent Identity</strong>: Formal attestation that this piece is NOT Deliverable 2."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-gate-c","title":"C — Deliverable 1 Competency Assessment","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"C — Deliverable 1 Competency Assessment","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] <strong>1. Complete Live Project Directory</strong>: <code>Deliverable_1_Session_Song/</code> containing the collected <code>.als</code> Set.","[ ] <strong>2. Exported 24-Bit Master WAV</strong>: <code>D1_Session_Master_v01.wav</code> (&gt; 2.0 minutes, no clipping, 44.1 kHz / 24-bit / POW-r 3).","[ ] <strong>3. Formally Named Scene Matrix</strong>: Minimum 6 to 8 named scenes matching a taught convention.","[ ] <strong>4. Written Scene Launch Chronology</strong>: <code>D1_SECTIONS.txt</code> documenting scene names, bar lengths, and Two-Lever Contrast verification."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
